## Pattern 0, share 01: across the yes posts

| Tag | Posts |
|---|---|
| tried | 22 of 31 |
| others | 6 of 31 |
| bought | 1 of 31 |
| feeling | 17 of 31 |

Tags use explicit statements by the speaker: tried includes completed preparations and consultations; others covers other adults' actions, advice or accounts, rather than the child's own behaviour or a shared attempt described only as “we”. Bought requires an explicit purchase or order; possession or use alone does not qualify. Feeling includes named curiosity, enjoyment and sensory aversion as well as distress. These counts describe posts in this share of pattern 0 from the supplied random sample of 20,000 posts, not people or the wider market. All 31 yes posts and all 213 near posts were read and individually tagged; nothing in the share remains unread.

### What they tried, in their words

- "We’ve tried different types of carriers and two types of strollers (bassinet attachment and the uppababy minu)." [sr007-0021]
- "I’m trying to expose her slowly and within her limits." [sr021-0088]
- "Hold him and hum the Mario Kart theme (he’s never seen it played or heard it)" [sr029-0109]
- "So I’m trying to encourage it again by doing lots of tummy time, but half the time he won’t lift his head because he’s too busy devouring his fingers." [sr038-0112]
- "We go to parks (I’ll baby wear her facing forward) and I wave at everyone (that looks friendly enough to wave back) to try and teach her this social gesture." [sr115-0127]
- "I called his doc and they told me to watch out for signs of head injuries, which made me worry even more." [sr059-0013]
- "I was slowly weaning my at the time 10month old off her pacifier, we were down to using it only to sleep." [sr063-0038]
- "she's already teetering on low iron (which I'm supplementing but I want her to get some nutritious meals in too)." [sr094-0063]
- "We're monitoring her weight ourselves at home with a baby scale. She's 5.5m." [sr033-0125]
- "Our 7.5 week old suddenly started rolling on his side so we realised we needed to stop swaddling and move onto sleep bags" [sr123-0045]

### What other people told them or did

- "When I look at videos online people talk about regular checks on baby's development etc. But the only time they last checked was at 8 weeks by the GP?" [sr033-0124]
- "My wife is amazing and very patient" [sr040-0073]
- "I called his doc and they told me to watch out for signs of head injuries, which made me worry even more." [sr059-0013]
- "My husband is okay with it and thinks he’ll break the habit when he is older." [sr075-0014]
- "The pediatrician and dentist aren’t concerned yet," [sr102-0043]
- "I read that a lot of parents would wean off around this age," [sr120-0020]

### What they bought or paid for

Only one yes post explicitly reports buying or ordering anything: two protective items in the same passage. The two excerpts below cover both items; the share does not supply five purchase quotes. Using or owning equipment is not treated as an explicit purchase.

- "I just ordered really thick and soft baby mats to put on my carpet," [sr068-0059]
- "I also ordered one of those backpack things that have  a pillow under his head if he falls." [sr068-0059]

### How they say they feel

- "I feel awful because I don’t want my wife to look at me as a failure, and she’ll never admit that to me, but there are times where I feel like I question whether or not I was ever cut out for this." [sr040-0073]
- "Staying strong and being the rock for my wife but I’m just anxious inside." [sr041-0001]
- "I have been an emotional wreck just constantly thinking about how these babies of ours are actually growing up before our eyes every single day." [sr049-0117]
- "I’m proud she feels confident enough to say no." [sr052-0109]
- "But the thought of happening is terrifying." [sr061-0141]
- "One day I had reached wits end" [sr090-0002]
- "I’m loving the baby stage way more than I ever expected." [sr106-0125]
- "I’m worried that she’ll start sucking her thumb for comfort as she still suckle her hands during the day while playing." [sr120-0020]
- "oh my god, I didn’t realise it would make me so sad lol!" [sr123-0045]

