### The parent needs practical arrangements for care, appointments, outings or a move.

14 of 213 posts.

Parents need workable childcare and household arrangements around naps, mobility and their own constraints, with stated ages from three months to nineteen months and some unknown. Questions include daycare contact naps, family events past bedtime, long-distance travel, fitting infant needs around an older child’s outings, a teenage babysitter and fear of childcare harm before the baby can speak. Others ask about lowering a crib despite back strain, using a public bathroom, moving home, caring for a walking toddler with a broken leg, or choosing convenient and informative paediatric appointments.

- "she certainly is going to have a big change in naps as the environment is so different with swaddling not allowed, a still active startle reflex, and her preference for contact naps." [sr001-0115]
- "My nanny will (paying her) but I doubt my family will. They’re already talking about breaking out the pack n play when I’m there. I know she needs to learn to sleep independently but I typically rescue those short crib naps with contact naps." [sr003-0094]
- "For those who’ve done a big time zone shift with a baby this age, how did you handle sleep when you arrived? Did you try to gradually adjust or just switch to local time right away?" [sr020-0145]
- "The crib has 3 depths, and we are already at the middle one. My wife has trouble getting him in and out as it is. Do I need to lower it to the bottom? I hate having him so far down (and the strain on our backs) but I don’t want him to pitch out headfirst." [sr035-0093]
- "So this might be a dumb question but if you’re out in the wild with your baby, alone, and you have to go to the bathroom and they’re sitting in the cart (not in their carrier, old enough to sit up on their own)… what do you do?" [sr064-0047]
- "I’m a SAHM who’s in school full time and I just need a break. My husband suggested daycare for a few days of the week but I’m unsure. I always see stuff about kids getting hurt by their teachers and I’m just so nervous about sending her somewhere where I won’t be. She can’t talk or walk yet so I won’t even be able to know if something happened to her. We have no help and my husband is usually gone before she wakes up and then gets home 2 hours before bedtime, so it’s just me and her for most of the day. I have so much anxiety about sending her off but I’m also overwhelmed and don’t know what to do. I would really appreciate advice." [sr114-0054]

**But:** An infant routine can work well with individual care but become difficult around sibling outings. "Started the same with the new baby and it is going great again, baby is happy all the time, getting full feeds, figuring out night time sleep really quickly. He’s on a bit of a nap schedule with 4 naps now and 7:30ish bedtime. Doing great with it and only waking up at 4a for a feed." [sr125-0059]

