### The parent wants safe, workable sleep as rolling or a new sleep setup changes the rules.

18 of 212 posts.

Posts run from newborns aged three weeks to toddlers of 14 and 23 months, alongside some ages that are unknown. Parents ask about stopping swaddling, leaving a self-rolled belly sleeper, moving from bedsharing to a crib, safer bedsharing ages, or fear after changing the sleep setup. The range includes a monitor false alarm and a parent who wants to stop bedsharing after accidental sleep in a chair.

- "I cant seem to sleep properly lately because of anxiety and worried that he might keep rolling back and I wouldnt notice." [sr118-0006]
- "Once babies start turning, you are not supposed to swaddle them anymore." [sr052-0114]
