### The parent asks what explains new or persistent night waking and whether it will pass.

36 of 213 posts.

Parents describe hourly or sleep-cycle waking, false starts, long awake spells, screaming, overnight poos and a toddler saying he is scared, and ask whether a regression, illness, teething or development explains it. Ages run from a 6.5-week-old to a 19-month-old, with some ages unknown. Some children previously slept long stretches, while others have never slept well; requests range from ways to cope and solidarity to reassurance that improvement can happen without a new intervention.

- "we've gone from bad sleep to awful sleep." [sr009-0084]
- "I think she’s overtired + her brain is going crazy from the new milestone that was reached + the pain from the teething and assuming a sore throat is what keeps her awake." [sr009-0031]
- "I asked him if he’s scared and he says yes. And he tells me he’s all done sleeping." [sr016-0039]
- "Well, it’s been falling apart the last few nights. Shorter and shorter stretches until last night was every 30-45 minutes. It’s the 4 month regression, I’m sure of it." [sr081-0075]
- "My 14 week old baby has started only sleeping in 4 hour chunks at night. This might sound great to some and I know it could be worse, but he was previously sleeping 8-10 hours uninterrupted." [sr129-0111]
- "My LO 14 months has been getting up religiously at 2 or 3, full of energy to play and then having a major crash out around the time he goes back to bed. What is this??" [sr133-0049]
