- "Everything I read online says his wake windows are way too long and that his bedtime should be between 7-8. My pediatrician told me to not rock the boat and just keep status quo since he’s growing well and his night sleep is solid." [sr034-0004]
- "I am so overwhelmed thinking that her wake windows are sometimes like 7 hours and she is getting like no naps during the day. I'm also worried about her not always getting to even the lower end of the 12-16 hours of sleep a day for her age. But she is pleasant, happy, rarely cranky, smiles all of the time, eats well and sleeps great at night." [sr051-0049]
- "when I see that he is having trouble sleeping for these long periods at night but not crying or calling out for me, should I be going in and helping him out or just let him figure it out?" [sr010-0117]
