- "I don’t know if i’m alone in this feeling but recently i wish i wasn’t a mother. I love my son to bits and would do anything for him but miss the freedom, and not having to worry 24/7 about my baby. I don’t like how i have so many responsibilities now." [sr113-0112]
- "At some point I woke up from a nightmare about him, I was hot, and I just broke down crying. I found myself grieving my old life — my independence, my mental space, the freedom of not having this constant responsibility. The physical weight of always being needed, having to do contact naps not knowing when it will end, always being "on"." [sr072-0060]
- "Last night however at 3am…I just lost it. Not at the baby, but I came out his room and woke my partner up in tears basically saying “I can’t do this! I need to f\*cking sleep…and I need to sleep without him touching me or kicking me, or having to hold him!! I don’t understand why he won’t sleep!!! I know it’s not his fault bit why won’t he f\*cking sleep I’ve done everything!”" [sr012-0181]
- "I use my son's nap to either get things done, or rest and recharge. With a second on the way, and knowing his nap length will just continue to decrease over time, it makes me anxious thinking about how my time to myself during the day will gradually just dissappear. Thanks for any advice or input!" [sr090-0126]
- "I just want to breathe. I want to figure out how to cope with this new life the best that I can. I am grieving my old life. I am grieving my marriage. I am grieving the old me." [sr088-0076]
- "My mom suggested clinical strength deodorant so I went to the store to get some. Let me tell you… best ten dollars I’ve spent." [sr029-0075]
- "And no one told me it would be painful to use tampons again!!? Just me!? I have had some scar tissue from my episiotomy and still having pain while doing the deed, but I didn’t even think about tampons… both in and out is torture, and pads give me too much of a familiar feeling to newly postpartum. Ugh." [sr054-0017]

**But:** One parent finds a solo week with one child unexpectedly spacious, even with a sleep regression. "And it reminded me how much down time there is with just 1 kid. The house has been clean the whole time, I’ve made some awesome meals, worked out daily. He even had a sleep regression this week, and it still felt like I had too much time. Anyone else experience this?" [sr064-0049]

