### The parent says new movement skills keep waking the baby or turning bedtime into play.

9 of 212 posts.

Rolling, pulling up, cruising and pre-crawling rocking appear in accounts from about 4–5 months through almost one year. Parents describe babies rolling into an unwanted position, standing instead of lying down, or climbing during lengthy settling. They ask how to prevent the repeated wake-and-resettle cycle or whether mastering another movement will help.

- "She screams when she rolls. She hasn’t learned to roll from stomach to back." [sr088-0094]
