### The parent wants to change naps, wake windows or bedtime to match the child's changing sleep.

15 of 212 posts.

From eight or ten weeks through about 20 months, these parents ask whether nap length, nap count, darkness, wake windows or bedtime need changing. Some children sleep well at night but refuse a late nap; others have early waking, false starts or short naps alongside night feeds. Parents compare tired cues with guidance and describe changes that sometimes worsen sleep.

- "what is the disadvantage of dropping to one early?" [sr039-0044]
- "Do I just wait till she shows signs of tiredness?" [sr071-0078]
- "I’ve tried for a couple nights getting him down earlier but that seems to make the night wake ups  more frequent." [sr088-0069]
- "Did you transition to 2 naps anyway or did they eventually just lengthen on their own?" [sr115-0042]
