### The parent wants an explanation or relief for symptoms that keep returning despite treatment.

5 of 213 posts.

These posts describe early teething, an ongoing cough, persistent gastrointestinal symptoms, newborn congestion and an 11-month-old's repeatedly broken or infected toenail. Children include a six-week-old, a three-month-old, an almost-five-month-old and a ten-month-old; parents link symptoms to sleep, feeding or mobility and describe doctors' responses, medicine and home attempts. They ask for causes, relief, other experiences or how hard to push, while worrying about medicine, pain or being dismissed. Medical and dosing statements remain the posters' accounts, not recommendations from this digest.

- "He's only 3 months old so most of the teething toys don't fit into his mouth and the ones that do he doesn't know how to frequently bite down yet so they don't work." [sr005-0072]
- "Well, only now I have come across the fact that OTC cough medicine for babies is not advised and I am feeling horrific mum guilt." [sr013-0185]
- "We’ve switched paediatricians three times and they all keep saying it’s probably a stomach virus." [sr021-0061]
- "We have a cool mist humidifier, use saline spray and nasal aspirator, sit in a steamy bathroom with a hot shower running, keep him upright for most of the day in a carrier. But none of this seems to be helping." [sr028-0041]
- "We did amoxicillin, turns out he has a reaction to that, stopped it per dr instructions. I was told keep it clean and trimmed. That’s what I’ve been doing !!!" [sr088-0072]

