Posts: 1sbhkc2 1sqek9e 1t1tszi 1t9os1s 1vkz4nh

### The parent wants milk feeds, digestion or weight gain to work better.

10 of 213 posts.

Parents report bottle-position dependence, pain and aversion, finger-sucking obscuring hunger cues, reflux when rolling, extra night hunger, stagnant weight and distress after a formula change. Ages include five- and nine-week-olds, a ten-week-old born at 36 weeks, a 14-week-old, four-, seven- and nine-month-olds and a walking 16-month-old. Attempts include different formula, bottles, nipple flows, feeding positions, more fats, upright holding, dairy elimination and medical advice; another parent struggles with relatives changing the feeding routine. They ask for workable feeds, whether intake or weight warrants concern, and experiences of a proposed appetite stimulant.

- "He’s had back to back teething and 2 ear infections in the last 6 weeks and this had caused the most severe feeding aversion yet, if he even sees the bottle he has a full meltdown." [sr036-0062]
- "We’ve tried increasing the nipple flow which we feel made her reflux worse, we’ve tried different bottles and nipples, different feeding positions, swaddling her while feeding, feeding in a dark quiet room, nothing seems to be working." [sr115-0103]
- "My seven month old only can take bottle feedings in a side lying position. At night he will sometimes accept another position but during the day, even if he has gone 4-5 hours without a bottle and is clearly hungry, he only wants to be on his side to eat." [sr017-0085]
- "Last night, she just went 12 hours without milk. Normally she gets up in about 6/7 hours and starts crying, but now she just wakes up and starts sucking her fingers." [sr049-0061]
- "She’s started walking in the past 2 months and never stops moving, and her weight has completely stagnated over this period and even dropped some. We’re trying all the things to bulk up fats, but I can’t force her to eat. This is a source of major stress and frustration for my family." [sr029-0004]
- "What worries me is simply that her weight seems to have completely plateaued for the last 10 days." [sr106-0099]
- "He’s passing 10 to 15 watery, explosive stools a day (lots of sharts) which triggered an intense, fiery diaper rash that flared up right after we switched his supplement from Enfamil Gentlease powder to Enfamil Gentleease Ready-to-Feed liquid." [sr119-0074]

**But:** One night-feeding worry ends with a different interpretation and improvement as solid-food intake rises: "Turns out she was just hungry! It was on and off for the last couple of months but she’s back to sleeping throughout the night now!" [sr074-0124]

