### The parent asks what the next stage will be like.

3 of 31 posts.

Parents of a calm 7.5-month-old and an enjoyable 4.5-month-old ask what toddlerhood may bring. A parent whose child is 23 months asks about the not-yet-arrived do-it-myself phase. They want experiences, funny stories and practical reflections about both good and difficult parts.

- "Our guy (7.5m) is super chill and I’d love a look into our future lol." [sr044-0069]
- "And how did that phase go for you as a whole?  Any funny stories or bits of wisdom?" [sr099-0067]
- "But I’m curious. What do you wish you knew about the toddler stage (1-3 years old) before you were in it?" [sr106-0126]
- "I’d love to hear your reflections — the good, the bad, any advice or pearls of wisdom." [sr106-0127]

**But:** One parent explicitly recognises that other people's experiences cannot determine this child's future: "I know all kids are different, but I’m curious what others with laid back little ones have experienced in toddlerhood!" [sr044-0069]

