5 of 31 posts.

These posts seek understanding, shared experience or reassurance about an individual baby’s temperament, from three months to nearly six months and a retrospective comparison with a second baby. They include relentless crying, a joking tally of a hard day, a search for other parents of high-need babies, curiosity about inherited temperament and uncertainty about being called “alert”.

- "My experience with my second is so so so different and I’ve done NOTHING different as a parent." [sr007-0060]
- "ich bin Mama eines High-Need-Babys. Mein Sohn ist jetzt knapp 6 Monate alt und da ich im Bekanntenkreis nur Leute mit Babys habe, die sich lächelnd im Kinderwagen an den Füßen spielen, bin ich auf der Suche nach Gleichgesinnten, die Lust auf etwas Austausch hätten :-)" [sr013-0082]
- "Minutes Crying: we forgot to count the minutes because we were holding our hands over our ears but your watch was telling you to leave the loud environment 3 times" [sr042-0036]
- "I'm curious if other parents also have a similar experience where you or your partner were as a baby/child is how your little one is." [sr088-0104]
- "My daughter is 4 months old. We are currently on holiday and everyone keeps commenting on how “alert” she is. I am a FTM so she is my only experience of a baby. What does this mean?!" [sr112-0060]

**But:** A calm baby also prompts the comparison. "[…] My baby (now 3 months) is pretty chill from what I gathered and also rarely cries." [sr088-0103]

