## Pattern 0, share 02: near posts

### The parent asks what changing sleep means and whether it will get easier.

53 of 213 posts.

These posts ask whether new waking, crying, nap refusal or feeding changes are a regression, illness, teething or a developmental change, and whether to wait or act. Ages run from newborn weeks to eighteen months, with some ages unknown; some parents dread the four-month regression before it starts, worry about too little or unusually long sleep, or cannot sleep themselves while anticipating a wake-up. Parents describe both modest changes and weeks or months of hourly waking, failed soothing, physical exhaustion and frustration at comparisons with easy sleepers. Others report improvement, while several say that independent settling or completed milestones have not secured uninterrupted nights.

- "This 8-10 month regression is absolutely NO joke. Holy moly. My baby slept through night from 4 months alllll the way up to 8 months and by golly gee, it feels like right on the 8 month marker my baby knew and hasn’t slept through the night in almost 3 months. This regression should be called the 8-10 month trenches. It’s literally the newborn trenches all over again. I’m not looking for advice or anything just solidarity on the struggle bus express." [sr027-0226]
- "I feel like I can’t enjoy these moments of growth because his sleep is so sensitive. Its one thing after another - crawling, babbling, etc. NON STOP. I am happy hes healthy and growing but I’ll get maybe 3 nights of good sleep before it gets ruined by something. I AM EXHAUSTED. My only friend with a baby right now has a unicorn sleeper and I’m so jealous." [sr039-0025]
- "[…] I am absolutely terrified of the four month regression. […]" [sr057-0083]
- "[…] Days she’s kept herself up later than she should, she’s slept great. Days she’s following everything down pat with her WW and naps, slept like shit." [sr052-0043]
- "My 3 week old has been fighting sleep SO hard the last few days and it makes me genuinely worried about any affects on him/his development? […]" [sr079-0086]
- "Coucou !! Je sais plus quoi faire !! Mon bébé ne s’endort JAMAIS !!! Elle se réveille à 21h et après veut pas dormir .. je suis dépourvu je passe des heures à essayer de l’endormir je trouve ça l’enfer .. elle s’endort à minuit/1h du matin .. avez vous des trucs .. depuis sa naissance elle régresse je sais plus où donner de la tête" [sr109-0142]
- "[…] Is this okay? I feel like she’s so little to be sleeping so long but I also feel like I might be doing that mom thing where I’m worrying instead of relaxing" [sr124-0100]

**But:** One parent reports an uninterrupted night after several difficult weeks. "Then last night….something magical ✨ happened. He slept from 10-6am without waking up once! Hopefully this is the turnaround! 🤞🏻" [sr100-0031]

